            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Baking Nana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love mushrooms and I loved this gravy. Warning though....I used salted butter - salted the mushrooms, as instructed and did not use low sodium beef broth. By the time the gravy had reduced it was a little salty for us. My fault entirely but just a heads up to others who will be making this. Delicious - Thanks Chef John."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Not a bad start, but much better if you add some drippings from the meat you serve this with - in my case it was Chef John's Classic Meatloaf. I also added a glug of red wine (Cabernet Sauvignon) and some minced shallots. I did use the optional fresh thyme and it was a nice addition. I'd recommend NO salt - there is quite enough in the beef stock.",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-07T19:34:15.740Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dranoel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Vegetarians listen up! I made this with vegetable broth. No matter, it was super. My vegetarian wife and I (the meat eater) loved it on mashed potatoes! If you want thicker gravy, use less broth.",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-14T17:01:11.263Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mamateach"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent! I think this gravy could be made even better with the addition of some wine...",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-26T10:47:34.073Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "polly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this a few times, just to be sure. Then made it for a wedding of 65 guest! I was given many excellent reviews. I really didn't know how important cooking out the moisture was until this video, no water no lumps, or at least that's how it played out. Be sure to cook the mushrooms all the way down, the flavor is great. I did add some good red wine for depth and color, but other than that it's a perfect Chef John recipe...again. OH, I did reheat it for the wedding and it came back to the correct thickness, so it can be made ahead.",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-15T12:51:28.963Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is amazingly delicious!! The only changes I made was to use vegetable stock instead of beef stock, and used 50g of flour to make it to the consistency that I liked. I served it over Chef John's mashed potatoes and my family loved it! This is going to be THE gravy from now on!",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-11T10:15:27.940Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan Moore"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like this recipe. I have adapted it by adding finely minced sauteed shallots, bay leaf, and 1 tsp red wine vinegar. I always season to taste, based on what I'm using it with, as I don't like too much salt.",
            "datePublished": "2024-09-03T21:12:38.995Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "J Valentine"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I absolutely love this recipe. Simple yet elegant. I used fresh shiitake mushrooms, delish! And I did add a little diced onion with the shrooms, I love onion in my gravy. FYI-be mindful of your salt; salting the shrooms, salty broth &amp; salted butter can be much for some. Make &amp; enjoy!",
            "datePublished": "2023-02-08T00:39:09.576Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TPATNO"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is great with boneless pork chops. Just brown the pork chops and pour gravy over them and bake. So easy. I don't put the whole quart of beef stock though. Just add a cup to start with and add as desired to get the right consistency.",
            "datePublished": "2023-02-22T22:13:26.694Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sdbfischer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good. Made basic recipe but tweaked it a bit by adding onions to mushrooms, not as much stock as indicated to get a thicker gravy, and a splash of white win for some of the stock. Definitely would make this again. Almost feel if I thinned it out, I'd have a great mushroom soup.",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-07T22:59:16.883Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Steve Heath"
            },
            "reviewBody": "OK, I made the same mistake as many first time I made it. It is too salty. However, I'm sure I know why. I used a boxed Beef Broth. As I was adding it, I tasted it (just the broth) and it was already WAY too salty. Chef John surely used homemade stock. \n\nIf you are using storebought stock, go for low sodium or omit the other salt. You can always add some back at the end if needed. Remember, the salt will concentrate as you reduce the gravy to thicken. Wait until final constancy to gauge if you need to add salt.\n\nNot his fault I went cheap and easy. \n\nOther than that, it tasted great. Cooking the flour gets you a nice smooth glossy gravy that looks like it was thickened with corn starch. Plus, no raw flour taste. \n\nI make first, then spoon over hamburger steaks, rice, mashed potatoes, as a topping for baked potatoes. Anywhere you can think.",
            "datePublished": "2021-06-12T21:36:37.877Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this exactly as the recipe says and it is amazing! We are Midwestern so have used it for Steak Hoagies, meatloaf, rice. It's so versatile. Has become a staple in my house.",
            "datePublished": "2026-10-08T22:10:45.781Z"
          },
